:: stage2-BFGRecap-vn-transcript-eng [nobr]
<p>Transcript:</p>
<p>So, there’s a little girl called Sophie, who is taken from her orphanage by the BFG - BFG stands for Big Friendly Giant. He collects and delivers sweet dreams to children with a special trumpet. </p>

<p>
    Then the BFG carries Sophie back to faraway Giant Country and there are other giants there. However, unlike the 9 other terrifying and enormous giants who eat humans, the BFG lives on Snozzcumbers. Remember the stain on the letter? 
    
</p>
<p>Sophie and BFG become friends and BFG teaches Sophie about how he keeps dreams in jars!</p>  

<p>However, the human-eating giants are planning to go eat so the BFG and Sophie hatch a brave plan to stop the human-eating giants by delivering a dream to the Queen (yes the Queen!) that will help prove their existence. When the Queen wakes up, Sophie is in her bedroom, further confirming the truth of the dream and she introduces the Queen to the BFG.</p> 

<p>The Queen agrees to help and, with the support of the army, the BFG and Sophie travel back to Giant Country and capture the man-eating giants with helicopters. The giants are taken away and the BFG is given a special title from the Queen - the ‘Royal Dream-Blower’.</p>


